  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "21463156",
      "title": "A First Summary",
      "lectureOrder": 22,
      "videoOrder": 18,
      "sourceHash": "cbef4ef26966330eea113d4e8ea2e984e9eaefee981a07976a634aafe94639c1",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.31,
          "end": 4.04,
          "en": "So, now before we dive",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.04,
          "end": 5.55,
          "en": "into our first practice",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.55,
          "end": 7.97,
          "en": "of those key features you learned about.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 7.97,
          "end": 10.48,
          "en": "It's all the time for our first brief summary",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 10.48,
          "end": 11.77,
          "en": "of what we learned.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 11.77,
          "end": 15.61,
          "en": "And we mostly learned about how to create Vue apps",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 15.61,
          "end": 20.49,
          "en": "and how to connect them to HTML code with mount.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 20.49,
          "end": 24.34,
          "en": "That you should use some unique CSS selector here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24.34,
          "end": 27.93,
          "en": "like here the ID selector because every Vue app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 27.93,
          "end": 32.38,
          "en": "can only be connected to one HTML element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 32.38,
          "end": 34.67,
          "en": "And you also see already that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 34.67,
          "end": 37.63,
          "en": "if you control an element with Vue,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 37.63,
          "end": 41.75,
          "en": "like here, where we are controlling this section with Vue.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 41.75,
          "end": 45.78,
          "en": "You automatically also control all child elements,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 45.78,
          "end": 48.53,
          "en": "but not any elements outside",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 48.53,
          "end": 51.72,
          "en": "of this Vue controlled section in this case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 51.72,
          "end": 55.86,
          "en": "So one Vue app can control one part in the HTML code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 55.86,
          "end": 57.93,
          "en": "but it then automatically controls",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 57.93,
          "end": 60.62,
          "en": "all child elements as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 60.62,
          "end": 64.68,
          "en": "Well, and in this Vue controlled HTML code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 64.68,
          "end": 66.73,
          "en": "you can use special features.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 66.73,
          "end": 71.46000000000001,
          "en": "Like this interpolation syntax with the double curly braces",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 71.46000000000001,
          "end": 75.46000000000001,
          "en": "or this binding syntax, this binding directive",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 75.46000000000001,
          "end": 80.42,
          "en": "with v-bind or v-html, as you also saw before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 80.42,
          "end": 82.97,
          "en": "These are features which are available",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 82.97,
          "end": 86.52,
          "en": "in that Vue controlled HTML code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 86.52,
          "end": 88.68,
          "en": "Now you can output data in there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 88.68,
          "end": 92.86,
          "en": "Therefore this interpolation, and this binding syntax",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 92.86,
          "end": 96.97999999999999,
          "en": "is also summarized under the term data binding.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 96.97999999999999,
          "end": 98.61,
          "en": "Because we're binding data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 98.61,
          "end": 103.61,
          "en": "which be managed in our Vue app to the HTML code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 103.75999999999999,
          "end": 105.65,
          "en": "either with the interpolation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 105.65,
          "end": 108.8,
          "en": "or with the v-bind directive syntax.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 108.8,
          "end": 110.7,
          "en": "And that's the important thing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 110.7,
          "end": 114.00999999999999,
          "en": "You pass an object to your Vue app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 114.00999999999999,
          "end": 115.97999999999999,
          "en": "which you create with createApp.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 115.97999999999999,
          "end": 119.11,
          "en": "And this object configures this app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 119.11,
          "end": 122.13,
          "en": "You can set various options for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 122.13,
          "end": 125.54,
          "en": "the data option or the methods option.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 125.54,
          "end": 127.18,
          "en": "Obviously we're going to learn about",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 127.18,
          "end": 128.79,
          "en": "other options for the course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 128.79,
          "end": 131.84,
          "en": "But these are two super important options",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 131.84,
          "end": 135.083,
          "en": "which you will probably meet in any app you're building.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 136.35,
          "end": 139.56,
          "en": "The data option takes a function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 139.56,
          "end": 141.03,
          "en": "therefore you can write it like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 141.03,
          "end": 144.64,
          "en": "Which should return an object full of data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 144.64,
          "end": 146.32999999999998,
          "en": "Which will then be available",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 146.32999999999998,
          "end": 151.03,
          "en": "in your Vue controlled HTML code, like vueLink here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 151.03,
          "end": 152.82,
          "en": "and which can also be accessed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 152.82,
          "end": 155.87,
          "en": "from inside your other parts of the Vue app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 155.87,
          "end": 159.44,
          "en": "Like the methods with the this keyword.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 159.44,
          "end": 161.32,
          "en": "Methods are also important.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 161.32,
          "end": 163.63,
          "en": "These are functions which you can call",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 163.63,
          "end": 167.92000000000002,
          "en": "from inside your Vue controlled HTML code, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 167.92000000000002,
          "end": 170.12,
          "en": "And that's what you'll learn about this far.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 171.03,
          "end": 175.57999999999998,
          "en": "Now, therefore, when we work with a framework like Vue,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 175.57999999999998,
          "end": 179.96,
          "en": "we typically say that we use a declarative approach",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 179.96,
          "end": 183.49,
          "en": "or that Vue uses a declarative approach.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 183.49,
          "end": 186.77,
          "en": "And that's just a fancy way of saying we,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 186.77,
          "end": 189.74,
          "en": "as a developer define the goal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 189.74,
          "end": 192.31,
          "en": "We define a template, you could say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 192.31,
          "end": 194.75,
          "en": "of the content we wanna have.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 194.75,
          "end": 199.35,
          "en": "We mark the parts which are dynamic like this one,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 199.35,
          "end": 201.61,
          "en": "or like this href attribute here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 201.61,
          "end": 203.53,
          "en": "which is bound with v-bind,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 203.53,
          "end": 207.25,
          "en": "and Vue will then do the rest for us.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 207.25,
          "end": 209.2,
          "en": "It does all the magic behind the scenes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 209.2,
          "end": 213.02,
          "en": "It outputs concrete values here and here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 213.02,
          "end": 214.98,
          "en": "And it updates the real DOM.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 214.98,
          "end": 218.59,
          "en": "Which is rendered to the screen and what the user sees",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 218.59,
          "end": 221.79,
          "en": "behind the scenes on our behalf.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 221.79,
          "end": 226.15,
          "en": "So we, as a developer just define the final picture",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 226.15,
          "end": 228.92000000000002,
          "en": "with the dynamic placeholders you could say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 228.92000000000002,
          "end": 231.039,
          "en": "and we don't define all the steps",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 231.039,
          "end": 233.85,
          "en": "of getting that picture onto the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 233.85,
          "end": 237.12,
          "en": "That's what we do with a framework like Vue.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 237.12,
          "end": 240.09,
          "en": "And that's why we also typically say",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 240.09,
          "end": 242.96,
          "en": "that Vue uses a declarative approach.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 242.96,
          "end": 245.73,
          "en": "We just declare our goal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 245.73,
          "end": 248.6,
          "en": "We don't care about the steps of getting there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 248.6,
          "end": 250.263,
          "en": "Now it's time to practice this.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
